From: OTB V5 <otb@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: do not reset before registration

An MCU timeout during the initial firmware load can happen before
mt76_register_device() has completed.  Scheduling reset_work from that path
can call ieee80211_restart_hw() while probe is unwinding and the hardware is
not registered, racing device teardown and causing a NULL dereference in
ieee80211_restart_work.

Only request the runtime reset once hardware initialisation has completed.
Probe-time timeouts still return -ETIMEDOUT and unwind normally; runtime MCU
timeouts retain the existing recovery behaviour.

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -229,7 +229,8 @@ mt7996_mcu_parse_response(struct mt76_dev
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Message %08x (seq %d) timeout\n",
 			cmd, seq);
 
-		if (!test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
+		if (dev->recovery.hw_init_done &&
+		    !test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
 			dev->recovery.restart = true;
 			wake_up(&dev->mt76.mcu.wait);
 			queue_work(dev->mt76.wq, &dev->reset_work);
